{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"a0c645d6e5dcfbd9284553c6cc94e8195c24d93f16bd2edbed5903c56f300bed","digest":{"component_or_area":"MCP blue-green autodeploy","key_entities":["AUTODEPLOY_ERROR","deploy_failed","AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP","AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT","rebar/host:deploy_errors","record_mcp_backoff_failure","record_mcp_routine_backoff","schedule_mcp_backoff","infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","infra/scripts/observability.sh","tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py"],"problem_keywords":["autodeploy","backoff","false alarm","deploy_errors","observability","port-exhausted","retire-cap","memory abort","mcp","blue-green"],"propositions":["Routine port-exhausted/retire-cap backoffs and low-memory aborts were incorrectly recorded as deploy failures, emitting AUTODEPLOY_ERROR and inflating the general deploy_errors alarm, violating the documented observability contract.","The fix separates routine backoff bookkeeping into schedule_mcp_backoff and record_mcp_routine_backoff, which write the backoff throttle file but do not emit deploy_failed markers.","Routine retire-cap backoffs must emit AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP and write the backoff file without triggering AUTODEPLOY_ERROR.","Routine low-memory aborts must emit AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT and write the backoff file without triggering AUTODEPLOY_ERROR.","Genuine MCP deploy failures must still emit AUTODEPLOY_ERROR with reason=deploy_failed to preserve the general deploy-failure alarm."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1788383064564886787,"uuid":"a8660be8-3463-4f14-a0a4-af7962f3a8db"}